{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"tool_UsXwDm0QLcyu5YlYIilOlnc9","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Progress\n     2→\n     3→## 2026-02-14 Session 5 (Requirement Capture)\n     4→\n     5→### Done\n     6→- Created `requirement-capture` openspec change with full artifacts\n     7→- Defined three-source requirement intake mechanism:\n     8→  - `autonomous-discovery`: Agent identifies need during implementation\n     9→  - `human-mcp`: Human responds to agent's request for input\n    10→  - `human-initiated`: Human proactively provides requirement (any interaction context)\n    11→- Clarified \"human-initiated\" includes both true interrupts and natural turn boundaries\n    12→- Created detailed usage examples for all three sources\n    13→- Archived change, applied `requirement-intake` spec to main specs/\n    14→- Updated status.md and progress.md\n    15→\n    16→### Changes\n    17→- `requirement-capture`: completed and archived\n    18→\n    19→### Open Issues\n    20→- None\n    21→\n    22→### Next Steps\n    23→- Use requirement-intake spec for new changes going forward\n    24→- Apply `[Source: ...]` markers in proposals to track requirement origins\n    25→\n    26→## 2026-02-14 Session 4 (Toolize SE 3.0)\n    27→\n    28→### Done\n    29→- Created `toolize-se3` openspec change with full artifacts (proposal → design → specs → tasks)\n    30→- Implemented 4 CLI tools via agent team parallel execution:\n    31→  - `se3 lint` - Validates spec format, required fields, WHEN/THEN scenarios\n    32→  - `se3 sync` - Synchronizes output/ with source (dry-run/apply/prune modes)\n    33→  - `se3 verify` - Pre-archive verification that scenarios are covered\n    34→  - `se3 status` - Session diagnostics with consistency checks\n    35→- All tools tested and working (se3 lint passes 9/9 specs)\n    36→- Archived change, applied 4 new specs to main specs/\n    37→- Added TOOLS.md documentation to output/\n    38→- Updated README wi