seline testing at startup, tests before commit\n    94→- Added spec guardrails to CLAUDE.md and CLAUDE.global.md: agents MUST NOT delete/weaken requirements, implementers MUST NOT modify the spec they implement against\n    95→- Added init.sh to startup protocol (Step 0) and project structure\n    96→- Updated best-practices.md with verification, guardrails, and init.sh sections\n    97→- Updated README.md with new principles and version history\n    98→\n    99→### Changes\n   100→- `v5-testing-guardrails-init`: completed\n   101→\n   102→### Open Issues\n   103→- None\n   104→\n   105→### Next Steps\n   106→- Test SE 3.0 v5.0 in a real project\n   107→- Validate verification protocol catches under-tested completions\n   108→- Validate spec guardrails prevent requirement drift\n   109→\n   110→## 2026-02-14 Session 1 (v4.1)\n   111→\n   112→### Done\n   113→- Added adaptive formality guidance to SDD section of CLAUDE.md\n   114→  - Large changes: full openspec workflow (proposal → specs → design → tasks)\n   115→  - Medium: brief proposal + tasks, specs if needed, skip design\n   116→  - Small: no openspec change, edit directly, update spec if behavior changed\n   117→- Positioned specs as agent contracts in agent team mode\n   118→- Added concrete role prompts for architect/implementer/reviewer\n   119→- Updated CLAUDE.global.md, README.md, best-practices.md\n   120→\n   121→### Changes\n   122→- All previous changes archived\n   123→- v4.1 applied directly (small change, no openspec change needed — practicing what we preach)\n   124→\n   125→### Open Issues\n   126→- None\n   127→\n   128→### Next Steps\n   129→- Test SE 3.0 v4.1 in a real project\n   130→- Validate agent team workflow with actual Task tool sub-agents\n   131→\n   132→## 2026-02-18 Session 6 (handoff)\n   133→\n   134→### Done\n   135→- Tool-enforced progress tracking: auto-generated progress.md, live se3 status, collab reports\n   136→- Update .claude/SE3.md to v1.10.0 with tool-enforced progres