{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"tool_LdRblSFcQD2lT4D3CXNo7g24","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# SE 3.0 — Software Engineering 3.0 Framework\n     2→\n     3→An AI-first long-horizon development framework for Claude Code.\n     4→\n     5→## Overview\n     6→\n     7→SE 3.0 combines Anthropic's [long-running agent best practices](https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/effective-harnesses-for-long-running-agents) with Spec Driven Development ([OpenSpec](https://github.com/Fission-AI/OpenSpec)) into a coherent system where AI agents drive development autonomously, calling humans only when needed.\n     8→\n     9→### Core Principles\n    10→\n    11→- **Human-as-MCP**: All human input (including initial project intent) obtained on-demand via human calls. Sync (ask directly) or async (write file). No pre-written requirement files.\n    12→- **Specs as Truth**: OpenSpec specs are the source of truth for **requirements**. In agent team mode, specs are contracts between agents.\n    13→- **Adaptive Formality**: Full openspec workflow for large changes; skip ceremony for small ones. Match process to scope.\n    14→- **Progressive Loading**: Sessions start with `progress.md` + `git log`. Everything else loads on demand.\n    15→- **Verify Before Done**: Never mark a feature complete without running tests. Spec scenarios are acceptance criteria.\n    16→- **Spec Guardrails**: Agents MUST NOT weaken or delete existing requirements without human approval.\n    17→- **Adaptive Conventions**: Commit when work is meaningful, clear context when saturated — not on mechanical schedules.\n    18→- **Native Agent Team**: Multi-agent via Claude Code's built-in Task tool. Specs serve as shared context for sub-agents.\n    19→\n    20→## Quick Start\n    21→\n    22→### 1. Install SE 3.0 CLI\n    23→\n    24→```bash\n    25→cd tools\n    26→pip install -e .\n    27→```\n    28→\n    29→### 2. Initialize a project\n    30→\n    31→```bash\n    32→mkdir my-project && cd my-project\n    33→git init\n    34→se3 init\n    35→```\n    36→\n    37→This creates:\n    38→\n    39→```\n    40→.claude/\n    41→├── CLAUDE.md    # Project-specific conventions (~25 lines)\n    42→└── SE3.md       # Complete SE 3.0 framework (~300 lines, managed by se3)\n    43→```\n    44→\n    45→### 3. Start developing\n    46→\n    47→Use the SE3 workflow skills:\n    48→\n    49→```\n    50→/se3:start   # Initialize session, check environment, load context\n    51→/se3:work    # Start or continue working on a change\n    52→/se3:done    # End session: tests, commit, handoff\n    53→```\n    54→\n    55→The agent will:\n    56→1. Run `se3 start --json` to compute session state and actions\n    57→2. Execute the returned actions (environment setup, baseline tests, etc.)\n    58→3. For `/se3:work`: Guide through bugfix/feature/review workflows with step tracking\n    59→4. For `/se3:done`: Run tests, commit changes, generate session summary\n    60→\n    61→All workflow logic is encoded in CLI commands that return JSON action arrays — the agent follows the program, not prose.\n    62→\n    63→### 4. Maintain SE3.md\n    64→\n    65→```bash\n    66→# Update to latest SE3 version\n    67→se3 update\n    68→```\n    69→\n    70→## Project Structure\n    71→\n    72→```\n    73→project/\n    74→├── init.sh                 # Environment setup (optional)\n    75→├── progress.md             # Cross-session history (auto-maintained by SE3 tools)\n    76→├── se3.config.yaml         # Configuration (optional)\n    77→├── README.md\n    78→├── human-calls/            # Async human call queue\n    79→├── tests/                  # Test files\n    80→├── tools/                  # CLI tools (se3 command)\n    81→├── .e2e-baselines/         # Visual regression baselines (optional)\n    82→├── openspec/\n    83→│   ├── specs/              # Source of truth for requirements\n    84→│   └── changes/\n    85→│       └── archive/\n    86→└── .claude/\n    87→    ├── CLAUDE.md           # Project-specific conventions (editable)\n    88→    ├── SE3.md              # SE 3.0 framework reference (managed by se3)\n    89→    └── commands/se3/       # Workflow skills: start.md, work.md, done.md\n    90→```\n    91→\n    92→## SE 3.0 CLI Tools\n    93→\n    94→SE 3.0 includes CLI tools to validate and enforce framework conventions:\n    95→\n    96→```bash\n    97→# Install tools\n    98→cd tools && pip install -e .\n    99→\n   100→# Initialize a new SE 3.0 project\n   101→se3 init\n   102→\n   103→# Validate specs\n   104→se3 lint\n   105→\n   106→# Sync output/ directory with source\n   107→se3 sync --dry-run   # Preview changes\n   108→se3 sync --apply     # Apply changes\n   109→\n   110→# Verify change implementation\n   111→se3 verify --change <change-name>\n   112→\n   113→# Diagnose session state\n   114→se3 status\n   115→\n   116→# Workflow driver commands (return JSON actions arrays)\n   117→se3 start --json       # Session initialization\n   118→se3 work --json        # List active changes or continue work\n   119→se3 work feature/auth --json   # Work on specific change\n   120→se3 done --json        # Session shutdown\n   121→\n   122→# Update SE3.md to latest version\n   123→se3 update\n   124→\n   125→# Commit with test verification\n   126→se3 commit -m \"Add feature\"\n   127→\n   128→# Multi-agent collaboration\n   129→se3 collab --daemon \"Implement feature\"\n   130→\n   131→# Show Claude command resolution\n   132→se3 claude-cmd\n   133→```\n   134→\n   135→See `output/TOOLS.md` for detailed documentation.\n   136→\n   137→## Key Concepts\n   138→\n   139→### Flow\n   140→\n   141→```\n   142→human call → openspec change (proposal → specs → code) → archive updates main specs\n   143→```\n   144→\n   145→Proposal captures intent, specs formalize it, archives preserve history. For small changes, skip the openspec workflow entirely — edit code, update spec if behavior changed, commit.\n   146→\n   147→### Session Protocol\n   148→\n   149→Progressive startup: `se3 status` (computed state) → `progress.md` (history) + `git log` → determine scope → load more only as needed. First-time: ask the human via human call.\n   150→\n   151→### Human-as-MCP\n   152→\n   153→| Mode | When | How |\n   154→|------|------|-----|\n   155→| Sync | Human present | Ask directly (AskUserQuestion) |\n   156→| Async | Human absent / offline action needed | Write to `human-calls/` |\n   157→\n   158→### SE3.md Module System\n   159→\n   160→SE 3.0 uses a two-file architecture to separate framework conventions from project-specific configurations:\n   161→\n   162→| File | Purpose | Editable | Managed by |\n   163→|------|---------|----------|------------|\n   164→| `.claude/SE3.md` | Complete SE 3.0 framework specification | ❌ No | `se3` CLI |\n   165→| `.claude/CLAUDE.md` | Project-specific conventions and overrides | ✅ Yes | Project team |\n   166→\n   167→This separation allows:\n   168→- **Framework updates**: `se3 update` updates SE3.md without touching project-specific configurations\n   169→- **Minimal project setup**: CLAUDE.md can be as short as 25 lines for simple projects\n   170→- **Version consistency**: SE3.md includes version and checksum for validation\n   171→\n   172→### Adaptive Conventions\n   173→\n   174→- **Commit**: When meaningful work is done. Not tied to /new.\n   175→- **Context clear**: When saturated or switching tasks. Not after every task group.\n   176→\n   177→### Agent Team\n   178→\n   179→Native Task tool. Parent spawns sub-agents per openspec change. Specs on the file system serve as contracts — sub-agents read them to know what to implement. Results return directly.\n   180→\n   181→## Output Files\n   182→\n   183→| File | Purpose |\n   184→|------|---------|\n   185→| `output/SE3.md.template` | SE3 framework template → `.claude/SE3.md` (via `se3 init`) |\n   186→| `output/CLAUDE.minimal.md.template` | Minimal CLAUDE.md template (25 lines) |\n   187→| `output/TOOLS.md` | CLI tools documentation |\n   188→| `docs/best-practices.md` | Best practices guide |\n   189→\n   190→## Version History\n   191→\n   192→### SE3 Framework Version\n   193→\n   194→| Version | Date | Changes |\n   195→|---------|------|---------|\n   196→| 2.4.0 | 2026-02-18 | Add `se3 full-cycle` command — runs complete start-work-done workflow in one command. Supports `--quick` flag for small tasks using 'small' workflow. Streamlines simple/quick tasks by combining session initialization, change creation, implementation, and shutdown. |\n   197→| 2.3.0 | 2026-02-18 | Merge CLAUDE.md into SE3.md, remove CLAUDE.md.template. Session Guard and simplified templates for 2.x manual trigger mode. |\n   198→| 2.2.0 | 2026-02-17 | Add Session Guard mechanism. `se3 work` and `se3 done` now check if session was started via `se3 start`. If not, return error with prompt to start session first. Simplified SE3.md.template and CLAUDE.md.template to reflect \"manual trigger\" philosophy (no longer expecting agent自觉性). |\n   199→| 2.1.0 | 2026-02-17 | Add Chinese language guidance to human calls context content. When language is set to Chinese (zh*), agent calls now include a note prompting humans to respond in Chinese, ensuring the entire interaction is localized. |\n   200→| 2.0.0 | 2026-02-17 | **BREAKING**: Programmatic workflow driver architecture. SE3.md reduced to ~80 lines (principles + entry points). All workflows encoded in CLI (`se3 start`, `se3 work`, `se3 done`) returning JSON actions arrays. Skills (`/se3:start`, `/se3:work`, `/se3:done`) are thin wrappers. Eliminates agent-interpreted prose in favor of CLI-driven execution. |\n   201→| 1.10.0 | 2026-02-17 | Tool-enforced progress tracking: `se3 commit` auto-appends to progress.md, `se3 handoff` generates session summaries, `se3 status` computes live state (removes status.md dependency), collab do_complete generates reports, worker FINDINGS.md convention\n   202→| 1.9.0 | 2026-02-17 | Add `se3 handoff` command — enforces commit-before-handoff rule, supports both direct usage (auto-commits) and collab mode (creates human-call)\n   203→| 1.8.8 | 2026-02-17 | Fix collab: archive old human-calls on startup, fix JSON extraction from manager, fix escalation output to stdout, limit manager turns to prevent verbose analysis loops\n   204→| 1.8.7 | 2026-02-17 | Fix: claude_runner temp .prompt files leaked due to unreachable cleanup code\n   205→| 1.8.6 | 2026-02-17 | Fix: collab orchestrator no longer exits when escalation happens before tasks exist\n   206→| 1.8.5 | 2026-02-17 | Fix: se3 update no longer writes back to output/SE3.md.template, preserving one-way data flow\n   207→| 1.8.4 | 2026-02-16 | Fix collab: detect_usage_limit() only checks last 3000 chars / 20 lines to avoid false positives from source code\n   208→| 1.8.3 | 2026-02-16 | Fix collab: detect_usage_limit() returns False when returncode=0 to avoid false positives from source code content\n   209→| 1.8.2 | 2026-02-16 | Fix: Resolve git merge conflict in claude_runner.py docstring\n   210→| 1.8.1 | 2026-02-16 | Fix framework version management: update SE3_FRAMEWORK_VERSION to 1.8.1, add version history entry\n   211→| 1.7.8 | 2026-02-16 | 优化 human calls 检测和处理机制：使用文件系统事件和缓存提升变更检测效率，增强响应完整性检查（重复内容检测、结构验证、长度限制），改进处理流程（批量处理、状态管理优化）\n   212→| 1.7.7 | 2026-02-16 | Fix collab: set max-turns to 0 (unlimited) instead of arbitrary limits; rely on timeout for control\n   213→| 1.7.6 | 2026-02-16 | Fix collab: increase manager max-turns from 3 to 10 (was hitting limit when reading files for planning)\n   214→| 1.7.5 | 2026-02-16 | Fix collab: use `@file` syntax for prompt passing to avoid CLI parsing issues (manager/worker launchers)\n   215→| 1.7.4 | 2026-02-16 | Fix collab: use `--output-format stream-json --verbose` for real-time output (enables activity-based timeout)\n   216→| 1.7.3 | 2026-02-16 | Fix collab: `-p` is a flag not an option; pass prompt as positional arg\n   217→| 1.7.2 | 2026-02-16 | Fix collab: remove bash alias support (too complex), remove error_max_turns from usage limit detection\n   218→| 1.7.1 | 2026-02-16 | Fix collab: support bash aliases/functions for claude commands (use bash -i)\n   219→| 1.7.0 | 2026-02-16 | Fix collab: skip missing commands (exit 127), improve JSON extraction from Claude envelope\n   220→| 1.6.9 | 2026-02-16 | Fix collab: add `error_max_turns` to usage limit detection (was preventing command switch)\n   221→| 1.6.8 | 2026-02-16 | Fix collab: launcher crash handling, select() EINTR handling, worker exit code capture\n   222→| 1.6.7 | 2026-02-16 | Fix collab: add YAML parse error warning; fix se3.config.yaml comment format\n   223→| 1.6.6 | 2026-02-16 | Fix collab: add \"hit your limit\" to usage limit detection keywords (was causing command not to switch)\n   224→| 1.6.5 | 2026-02-16 | Fix collab: manager launcher outputs valid JSON on failure, signal handling moved to launcher, import error handling, escalation JSON\n   225→| 1.6.4 | 2026-02-16 | Fix collab launchers: JSON extraction, race conditions, signal handling, task dir creation, stderr handling |\n   226→| 1.6.3 | 2026-02-16 | Fix collab orchestrator: manager now uses activity-based monitoring via launcher, proper limit detection |\n   227→| 1.6.2 | 2026-02-16 | Fix collab orchestrator: treat `error_max_turns` as usage limit and switch command |\n   228→| 1.6.1 | 2026-02-16 | Fix collab orchestrator: clear CLAUDECODE on daemon start, command switch on JSON parse error |\n   229→| 1.6.0 | 2026-02-16 | Activity-based timeout for collab workers: real-time I/O monitoring, automatic command fallback on inactivity, `run_with_monitor()` API |\n   230→| 1.5.5 | 2026-02-16 | Fix collab orchestrator: extract JSON from Claude CLI envelope via Python, add --dangerously-skip-permissions for daemon mode, reduce manager max-turns |\n   231→| 1.5.4 | 2026-02-16 | Fix do_plan: use Python for task extraction instead of jq-complete (which lacks length/iteration support) |\n   232→| 1.5.3 | 2026-02-16 | Fix collab orchestrator: clean stale tasks on new session, handle empty task list, do_plan supports full tasks array |\n   233→| 1.5.2 | 2026-02-16 | Fix collab manager: use text output format, strip markdown fences from Claude response before JSON parsing |\n   234→| 1.5.1 | 2026-02-16 | Fix collab daemon: pass objective to orchestrator script, clear CLAUDECODE env to prevent nested session error |\n   235→| 1.5.0 | 2026-02-16 | Simplified collab: removed External Controller v2 (daemon, API, MCP). Bash orchestrator only. File-based async communication. |\n   236→| 1.4.0 | 2026-02-16 | Claude Command Resolver: priority-based multi-command fallback on usage limit/timeout, unified config module, `se3 claude-cmd` CLI |\n   237→| 1.3.0 | 2026-02-16 | Complete External Controller: MCP server, HTTP API, session persistence, auto-commit, collab v2 integration |\n   238→| 1.2.0 | 2026-02-16 | External Controller: session daemon with auto-commit, collaboration outside Claude (fixes nested process limitation) |\n   239→| 1.1.2 | 2026-02-16 | Fix collab orchestrator: jq-complete pipe assignments (`|`) and `+=` operator, MOCK_MODE unbound variable |\n   240→| 1.1.1 | 2026-02-16 | Version management module with strict enforcement rules |\n   241→| 1.1.0 | 2026-02-16 | Git Worktree Collaboration: independent entry mode (`--daemon`, `--manual`), multi-language human calls, version consistency check |\n   242→| 1.0.0 | 2026-02-16 | Initial stable release: `se3 init`, `se3 update`, `se3 commit`, `se3 collab`, Semantic Versioning 2.0.0 |\n   243→\n   244→<details>\n   245→<summary>Pre-1.0 Development History (archived)</summary>\n   246→\n   247→- v7.0 — 2026-02-14 — SE3 Module System: Separate framework (SE3.md) from project config (CLAUDE.md), `se3 init` command\n   248→- v6.1 — 2026-02-14 — Requirement intake: three-source taxonomy for structured requirement capture\n   249→- v6.0 — 2026-02-14 — CLI tools: se3 lint, sync, verify, status for enforceable framework\n   250→- v5.1 — 2026-02-14 — Diagnostic dashboard: status.md for single-source-of-truth session state\n   251→- v5.0 — 2026-02-14 — Verification protocol, spec guardrails, init.sh environment automation\n   252→- v4.1 — 2026-02-14 — Adaptive formality: match SDD ceremony to change scope\n   253→- v4.0 — 2026-02-14 — Remove demands.md, specs as truth, adaptive commit/context rules\n   254→- v3.0 — 2026-02-14 — English rewrite, native agent team, global CLAUDE.md\n   255→- v2.0 — 2026-02-14 — Remove intentions.md, unified Human-as-MCP, progressive startup\n   256→- v1.0 — 2026-02-14 — Initial concept\n   257→\n   258→</details>\n   259→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"tool_Es7mxUkJda2Fynqc4h0KnPJS","session_id":"aa649a33-92f6-4c3e-90ea-c763bdcdac3a","uuid":"22356739-399f-4539-8354-fe72114e8c6b"}
