/changes/archive/2026-02-14-toolize-se3/specs/status-diagnostics","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"tool_Es7mxUkJda2Fynqc4h0KnPJS","session_id":"aa649a33-92f6-4c3e-90ea-c763bdcdac3a","uuid":"57a5fdf7-bc6a-4b58-93f3-7c499c9f05de"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"tool_Es7mxUkJda2Fynqc4h0KnPJS","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the SE3 codebase. Let me provide a detailed summary.\n\n## Comprehensive SE3 Codebase Analysis\n\n### Project Purpose and Architecture\n\n**SE 3.0 (Software Engineering 3.0)** is an AI-first long-horizon development framework for Claude Code that combines Anthropic's long-running agent best practices with Spec Driven Development (OpenSpec). The project is currently in **bootstrapping mode** - it uses existing SE3 specifications to develop the next generation of SE3.\n\n**Core Philosophy:**\n- **Human-as-MCP**: All human input obtained on-demand via sync (direct ask) or async (file-based) human calls\n- **Specs as Truth**: OpenSpec specs are the source of truth for requirements and contracts between agents\n- **Adaptive Formality**: Full openspec workflow for large changes, skip ceremony for small ones\n- **Progressive Loading**: Sessions start with minimal context, load more on demand\n- **Verify Before Done**: Never mark complete without running tests\n\n**Architecture Components:**\n1. **CLI Tools** (`tools/se3_tools/`): Python-based CLI with commands like `se3 start`, `se3 work`, `se3 done`, `se3 lint`, `se3 commit`, `se3 collab`\n2. **Specs Directory** (`openspec/specs/`): 13 specification modules defining framework behavior\n3. **Changes Archive** (`openspec/changes/archive/`): Completed changes with full artifacts (proposal → specs → design → tasks)\n4. **Collaboration System** (`.collab/`): Git worktree-based multi-agent collaboration with bash orchestrator\n5. **Output Templates** (`output/`): Templates for `se3 init` (SE3.md.template, CLAUDE.md.template)\n\n---\n\n### Existing Specs and Their Status\n\nThe `openspec/specs/` directory contains **13 specification modules**:\n\n| Spec | Purpose | Status | Completeness |\n|------|---------|--------|--------------|\n| **agent-team** | Multi-agent coordination via Task tool | Complete | Full spec with scenarios |\n| **change-verifier** | Verify implementation covers spec scenarios | Complete | Has scenarios for extraction and detection |\n| **git-worktree-collab** | Simplified v2 collaboration (bash orchestrator) | Complete | Comprehensive, includes migration from v2 |\n| **human-as-mcp** | Human call interface (sync/async) | Complete | Full spec with first-time bootstrap |\n| **output-sync** | Template management for se3 init | Complete | Simple but complete |\n| **requirement-intake** | Three-source requirement taxonomy | **TBD Purpose** | Complete scenarios, needs purpose filled |\n| **se3-config** | Configuration system (se3.config.yaml) | Complete | Full spec with all options |\n| **se3-controller** | External controller API (OpenAPI spec) | **Experimental** | YAML spec, marked for removal in v2 |\n| **se3-module-system** | Framework/project separation | Complete | Defines CLAUDE.md + SE3.md architecture |\n| **se3-scaffold** | Project initialization and templates | Complete | Comprehensive, includes CLI tools list |\n| **session-protocol** | Session lifecycle (startup/execution/shutdown) | Complete | Includes tool-enforced progress tracking |\n| **spec-lint** | Spec file validation | **TBD Purpose** | Complete scenarios, needs purpose filled |\n| **status-diagnostics** | Real-time status from live state | Complete | Replaces manual status.md |\n\n**Note:** Two specs have \"TBD - created by archiving change\" in their Purpose field and need to be updated: `requirement-intake` and `spec-lint`.\n\n---\n\n### What Features Are Complete vs Incomplete\n\n#### **COMPLETE Features:**\n\n**CLI Tools (All Implemented):**\n- `se3 init` - Initialize SE 3.0 project\n- `se3 start` - Session initialization with JSON action arrays\n- `se3 work` - SDD development workflows (bugfix/feature/review/directive/small)\n- `se3 done` - Session shutdown with handoff\n- `se3 lint` - Validate spec format and scenarios\n- `se3 sync` - Synchronize output/ directory\n- `se3 verify` - Verify change implementation covers scenarios\n- `se3 status` - Real-time project diagnostics\n- `se3 update` - Update SE3.md to latest version\n- `se3 commit` - Commit with test verification\n- `se3 collab` - Multi-agent collaboration (bash orchestrator)\n- `se3 handoff` - Generate session summary\n- `se3 claude-cmd` - Show configured Claude commands\n- `se3 full-cycle` (v2.4.0) - Complete start-work-done workflow in one command\n\n**Workflow Drivers:**\n- Start command encodes 7-step startup protocol\n- Work command encodes all SDD workflows with step tracking\n- Done command encodes shutdown protocol\n- All return JSON action arrays for agent execution\n\n**Collaboration System:**\n- Git worktree-based isolation\n- Bash orchestrator (collab-orchestrator.sh)\n- Manager and worker launchers\n- File-based async communication\n- Task lifecycle management (pending → in_progress → done/failed/blocked/timeout)\n- Human call integration for blocked workers\n\n**Progress Tracking:**\n- `se3 commit` auto-appends to progress.md\n- `se3 handoff` generates formal session records\n- `se3 status` computes live state\n- Collab reports generated by orchestrator\n\n**Configuration:**\n- Project-level se3.config.yaml\n- Global ~/.se3/config.yaml support\n- Priority-based Claude command resolution\n\n---\n\n#### **INCOMPLETE / REMAINING Features:**\n\nBased on the `issues.md` file and spec analysis, the following functionality remains to be implemented:\n\n**1. OpenSpec Integration (Critical Gap)**\n```\nIssue: \"你确定openspec的init加到了流程中吗？为什么这么久了这个项目还是没有init后的openspec commands？\"\n```\n- The session-protocol spec references `openspec init` and `openspec list --specs`\n- However, no `openspec` CLI tool exists in the codebase\n- **This is a significant gap**: The framework references OpenSpec commands but they don't exist\n\n**2. Human Call Enhancements:**\n- Archive human calls (currently only tracked in human-calls/ directory)\n- Human input methods beyond MCP calls and running Claude (e.g., prompt files)\n- Better human call status visibility in `se3 collab --status`\n\n**3. Version Management:**\n- Clarify SE3.md version vs CLI tool version\n- Currently at version 2.4.0 (framework) but version management is unclear\n- Need unified versioning strategy\n\n**4. Progress.md in Commit Flow:**\n```\nIssue: \"progress.md的修改似乎在提交之前，是否要将它加入到提交流程中\"\n```\n- Progress.md is auto-modified by tools but may need explicit commit handling\n\n**5. SE3.md vs Help Documentation:**\n```\nIssue: \"SE3.md没有存在的意义，文档可以加到se3的帮助里，但是需要有地方记录已安装的commands的版本\"\n```\n- Debate about whether SE3.md should exist or be replaced by `se3 help`\n- Need version tracking for installed commands\n\n**6. External Controller (Deprecated/Removed):**\n- The `se3-controller/spec.yaml` defines an HTTP API and daemon\n- Git worktree collab spec says this is removed in v2\n- **Migration needed**: Remove or archive the external controller spec\n\n**7. Missing Purpose Fields:**\n- `requirement-intake/spec.md`: Has \"TBD - created by archiving change\"\n- `spec-lint/spec.md`: Has \"TBD - created by archiving change\"\n- `change-verifier/spec.md`: Has \"TBD - created by archiving change\"\n\n**8. Test Coverage:**\n- Tests exist for collab, commit, human_calls, progress, claude_runner\n- Need to verify all specs have corresponding test coverage\n- The `se3 verify` command exists but may not be fully integrated\n\n---\n\n### What \"Remaining SE3 Functionality\" Likely Refers To\n\nBased on the issues and gaps identified:\n\n**Immediate Priority:**\n1. **OpenSpec CLI Implementation**: The framework assumes `openspec` commands exist but they don't\n2. **Spec Purpose Updates**: Fill in TBD purposes for 3 specs\n3. **Remove/Archive External Controller**: Clean up the deprecated se3-controller spec\n4. **Human Call Archiving**: Implement archival of completed human calls\n\n**Medium Priority:**\n5. **Version Management Strategy**: Clarify CLI vs framework versions\n6. **Progress.md Commit Integration**: Ensure progress.md changes are properly committed\n7. **SE3.md vs Help System**: Decide on documentation architecture\n\n**Architectural Questions:**\n8. **OpenSpec Commands**: The framework references commands like `openspec init`, `openspec list`, but these may need to be implemented as part of `se3` CLI instead\n9. **Human Input Methods**: Expand beyond sync/async human calls to support file-based input\n10. **Command Version Tracking**: Track versions of installed commands separately from framework version\n\n---\n\n### Project Structure Summary\n\n```\n/data/cre/workspace/se3.0/\n├── openspec/specs/          # 13 specification modules (source of truth)\n├── openspec/changes/archive/# 6 archived changes with full artifacts\n├── tools/se3_tools/         # CLI implementation (Python)\n│   ├── commands/            # Individual command modules\n│   ├── cli.py              # Main CLI entry point\n│   ├── human_calls.py      # Human call management\n│   └── progress.py         # Progress tracking\n├── scripts/                 # Bash orchestrator and collab scripts\n├── tests/                   # Test suite (pytest)\n├── output/                  # Templates for se3 init\n├── .claude/                 # Project's own SE3 configuration\n│   ├── CLAUDE.md           # Project-specific conventions\n│   └── SE3.md              # Framework reference (v2.3.0)\n├── progress.md             # Cross-session progress tracking\n├── status.md               # Runtime dashboard (now computed)\n└── issues.md               # Active and old issues (in Chinese)\n```\n\nThe project is highly structured and well-documented, with most core functionality implemented. The main gaps are the OpenSpec CLI integration, spec purpose completion, and resolution of architectural questions documented in issues.md."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: abef50a (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 56115\ntool_uses: 36\nduration_ms: 63625</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aa649a33-92f6-4c3e-90ea-c763bdcdac3a","uuid":"573561fc-8ac5-4a17-8a9b-0a97667b3d45","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the SE3 codebase at /data/cre/workspace/se3.0 to understand:\n1. What is the project structure?\n2. What specs exist in openspec/specs/ directory?\n3. What functionality has been implemented vs what remains?\n4. Look for any TODO files, progress tracking, or incomplete features\n\nProvide a comprehensive summary of:\n- Project purpose and architecture\n- Existing specs and their status\n- What features are complete vs incomplete\n- What the \"remaining SE3 functionality\" likely refers to","agentId":"abef50a","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the SE3 codebase. Let me provide a detailed summary.\n\n## Comprehensive SE3 Codebase Analysis\n\n### Project Purpose and Architecture\n\n**SE 3.0 (Software Engineering 3.0)** is an AI-first long-horizon development framework for Claude Code that combines Anthropic's long-running agent best practices with Spec Driven Development (OpenSpec). The project is currently in **bootstrapping mode** - it uses existing SE3 specifications to develop the next generation of SE3.\n\n**Core Philosophy:**\n- **Human-as-MCP**: All human input obtained on-demand via sync (direct ask) or async (file-based) human calls\n- **Specs as Truth**: OpenSpec specs are the source of truth for requirements and contracts between agents\n- **Adaptive Formality**: Full openspec workflow for large changes, skip ceremony for small ones\n- **Progressive Loading**: Sessions start with minimal context, load more on demand\n- **Verify Before Done**: Never mark complete without running tests\n\n**Architecture Components:**\n1. **CLI Tools** (`tools/se3_tools/`): Python-based CLI with commands like `se3 start`, `se3 work`, `se3 done`, `se3 lint`, `se3 commit`, `se3 collab`\n2. **Specs Directory** (`openspec/specs/`): 13 specification modules defining framework behavior\n3. **Changes Archive** (`openspec/changes/archive/`): Completed changes with full artifacts (proposal → specs → design → tasks)\n4. **Collaboration System** (`.collab/`): Git worktree-based multi-agent collaboration with bash orchestrator\n5. **Output Templates** (`output/`): Templates for `se3 init` (SE3.md.template, CLAUDE.md.template)\n\n---\n\n### Existing Specs and Their Status\n\nThe `openspec/specs/` directory contains **13 specification modules**:\n\n| Spec | Purpose | Status | Completeness |\n|------|---------|--------|--------------|\n| **agent-team** | Multi-agent coordination via Task tool | Complete | Full spec with scenarios |\n| **change-verifier** | Verify implementation covers spec scenarios | Complete | Has scenarios for extraction and detection |\n| **git-worktree-collab** | Simplified v2 collaboration (bash orchestrator) | Complete | Comprehensive, includes migration from v2 |\n| **human-as-mcp** | Human call interface (sync/async) | Complete | Full spec with first-time bootstrap |\n| **output-sync** | Template management for se3 init | Complete | Simple but complete |\n| **requirement-intake** | Three-source requirement taxonomy | **TBD Purpose** | Complete scenarios, needs purpose filled |\n| **se3-config** | Configuration system (se3.config.yaml) | Complete | Full spec with all options |\n| **se3-controller** | External controller API (OpenAPI spec) | **Experimental** | YAML spec, marked for removal in v2 |\n| **se3-module-system** | Framework/project separation | Complete | Defines CLAUDE.md + SE3.md architecture |\n| **se3-scaffold** | Project initialization and templates | Complete | Comprehensive, includes CLI tools list |\n| **session-protocol** | Session lifecycle (startup/execution/shutdown) | Complete | Includes tool-enforced progress tracking |\n| **spec-lint** | Spec file validation | **TBD Purpose** | Complete scenarios, needs purpose filled |\n| **status-diagnostics** | Real-time status from live state | Complete | Replaces manual status.md |\n\n**Note:** Two specs have \"TBD - created by archiving change\" in their Purpose field and need to be updated: `requirement-intake` and `spec-lint`.\n\n---\n\n### What Features Are Complete vs Incomplete\n\n#### **COMPLETE Features:**\n\n**CLI Tools (All Implemented):**\n- `se3 init` - Initialize SE 3.0 project\n- `se3 start` - Session initialization with JSON action arrays\n- `se3 work` - SDD development workflows (bugfix/feature/review/directive/small)\n- `se3 done` - Session shutdown with handoff\n- `se3 lint` - Validate spec format and scenarios\n- `se3 sync` - Synchronize output/ directory\n- `se3 verify` - Verify change implementation covers scenarios\n- `se3 status` - Real-time project diagnostics\n- `se3 update` - Update SE3.md to latest version\n- `se3 commit` - Commit with test verification\n- `se3 collab` - Multi-agent collaboration (bash orchestrator)\n- `se3 handoff` - Generate session summary\n- `se3 claude-cmd` - Show configured Claude commands\n- `se3 full-cycle` (v2.4.0) - Complete start-work-done workflow in one command\n\n**Workflow Drivers:**\n- Start command encodes 7-step startup protocol\n- Work command encodes all SDD workflows with step tracking\n- Done command encodes shutdown protocol\n- All return JSON action arrays for agent execution\n\n**Collaboration System:**\n- Git worktree-based isolation\n- Bash orchestrator (collab-orchestrator.sh)\n- Manager and worker launchers\n- File-based async communication\n- Task lifecycle management (pending → in_progress → done/failed/blocked/timeout)\n- Human call integration for blocked workers\n\n**Progress Tracking:**\n- `se3 commit` auto-appends to progress.md\n- `se3 handoff` generates formal session records\n- `se3 status` computes live state\n- Collab reports generated by orchestrator\n\n**Configuration:**\n- Project-level se3.config.yaml\n- Global ~/.se3/config.yaml support\n- Priority-based Claude command resolution\n\n---\n\n#### **INCOMPLETE / REMAINING Features:**\n\nBased on the `issues.md` file and spec analysis, the following functionality remains to be implemented:\n\n**1. OpenSpec Integration (Critical Gap)**\n```\nIssue: \"你确定openspec的init加到了流程中吗？为什么这么久了这个项目还是没有init后的openspec commands？\"\n```\n- The session-protocol spec references `openspec init` and `openspec list --specs`\n- However, no `openspec` CLI tool exists in the codebase\n- **This is a significant gap**: The framework references OpenSpec commands but they don't exist\n\n**2. Human Call Enhancements:**\n- Archive human calls (currently only tracked in human-calls/ directory)\n- Human input methods beyond MCP calls and running Claude (e.g., prompt files)\n- Better human call status visibility in `se3 collab --status`\n\n**3. Version Management:**\n- Clarify SE3.md version vs CLI tool version\n- Currently at version 2.4.0 (framework) but version management is unclear\n- Need unified versioning strategy\n\n**4. Progress.md in Commit Flow:**\n```\nIssue: \"progress.md的修改似乎在提交之前，是否要将它加入到提交流程中\"\n```\n- Progress.md is auto-modified by tools but may need explicit commit handling\n\n**5. SE3.md vs Help Documentation:**\n```\nIssue: \"SE3.md没有存在的意义，文档可以加到se3的帮助里，但是需要有地方记录已安装的commands的版本\"\n```\n- Debate about whether SE3.md should exist or be replaced by `se3 help`\n- Need version tracking for installed commands\n\n**6. External Controller (Deprecated/Removed):**\n- The `se3-controller/spec.yaml` defines an HTTP API and daemon\n- Git worktree collab spec says this is removed in v2\n- **Migration needed**: Remove or archive the external controller spec\n\n**7. Missing Purpose Fields:**\n- `requirement-intake/spec.md`: Has \"TBD - created by archiving change\"\n- `spec-lint/spec.md`: Has \"TBD - created by archiving change\"\n- `change-verifier/spec.md`: Has \"TBD - created by archiving change\"\n\n**8. Test Coverage:**\n- Tests exist for collab, commit, human_calls, progress, claude_runner\n- Need to verify all specs have corresponding test coverage\n- The `se3 verify` command exists but may not be fully integrated\n\n---\n\n### What \"Remaining SE3 Functionality\" Likely Refers To\n\nBased on the issues and gaps identified:\n\n**Immediate Priority:**\n1. **OpenSpec CLI Implementation**: The framework assumes `openspec` commands exist but they don't\n2. **Spec Purpose Updates**: Fill in TBD purposes for 3 specs\n3. **Remove/Archive External Controller**: Clean up the deprecated se3-controller spec\n4. **Human Call Archiving**: Implement archival of completed human calls\n\n**Medium Priority:**\n5. **Version Management Strategy**: Clarify CLI vs framework versions\n6. **Progress.md Commit Integration**: Ensure progress.md changes are properly committed\n7. **SE3.md vs Help System**: Decide on documentation architecture\n\n**Architectural Questions:**\n8. **OpenSpec Commands**: The framework references commands like `openspec init`, `openspec list`, but these may need to be implemented as part of `se3` CLI instead\n9. **Human Input Methods**: Expand beyond sync/async human calls to support file-based input\n10. **Command Version Tracking**: Track versions of installed commands separately from framework version\n\n---\n\n### Project Structure Summary\n\n```\n/data/cre/workspace/se3.0/\n├── openspec/specs/          # 13 specification modules (source of truth)\n├── openspec/changes/archive/# 6 archived changes with full artifacts\n├── tools/se3_tools/         # CLI implementation (Python)\n│   ├── commands/            # Individual command modules\n│   ├── cli.py              # Main CLI entry point\n│   ├── human_calls.py      # Human call management\n│   └── progress.py         # Progress tracking\n├── scripts/                 # Bash orchestrator and collab scripts\n├── tests/                   # Test suite (pytest)\n├── output/                  # Templates for se3 init\n├── .claude/                 # Project's own SE3 configuration\n│   ├── CLAUDE.md           # Project-specific conventions\n│   └── SE3.md              # Framework reference (v2.3.0)\n├── progress.md             # Cross-session progress tracking\n├── status.md               # Runtime dashboard (now computed)\n└── issues.md               # Active and old issues (in Chinese)\n```\n\nThe project is highly structured and well-documented, with most core functionality implemented. The main gaps are the OpenSpec CLI integration, spec purpose completion, and resolution of architectural questions documented in issues.md."}],"totalDurationMs":63625,"totalTokens":56115,"totalToolUseCount":36,"usage":{"input_tokens":1978,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":51968,"output_tokens":2169,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
