{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"tool_DzK8izq7JhpZtpnoDsJ75O0s","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# human-as-mcp Specification\n     2→\n     3→## Purpose\n     4→Define the Human-as-MCP interface for obtaining human input on-demand. This spec governs sync and async human call modes, call persistence, non-blocking execution, and the first-time bootstrap flow where project intent is captured directly from human input without pre-written requirement files.\n     5→## Requirements\n     6→### Requirement: Human Call Interface\n     7→The system SHALL define a standard human call interface supporting sync and async modes.\n     8→\n     9→**Sync mode** (human present):\n    10→- Ask directly via Claude Code conversation (AskUserQuestion)\n    11→- Use for: immediate decisions, requirement clarification, project direction\n    12→\n    13→**Async mode** (human unavailable):\n    14→- Write request file to `human-calls/`\n    15→- Use for: offline operations, cross-session pending requests\n    16→\n    17→**First-time bootstrap**: When entering an empty project, the agent SHALL ask the human \"What should this project do?\" via sync human call, then create an openspec change directly from the response. The change proposal captures the human's intent; specs formalize it. No intermediate demands file.\n    18→\n    19→#### Scenario: Sync call — first-time project intent\n    20→- **WHEN** agent enters an empty project\n    21→- **THEN** agent asks the human via sync call, creates an openspec change proposal from the response\n    22→\n    23→#### Scenario: Sync call — immediate decision\n    24→- **WHEN** agent needs a human decision and the human is present\n    25→- **THEN** agent asks directly via conversation\n    26→\n    27→#### Scenario: Async call — offline operation\n    28→- **WHEN** agent needs the human to perform an operation that requires offline time\n    29→- **THEN** agent writes a request to human-calls/, marks dependent tasks as waiting-human\n    30→\n    31→#### Scenario: Human responds to async call\n    32→- **WHEN** a human fills in the Response section of a pending request\n    33→- **THEN** next session processes the response and unblocks dependent work\n    34→\n    35→### Requirement: Non-Blocking Execution\n    36→Human calls MUST NOT block unrelated tasks.\n    37→\n    38→#### Scenario: Continue after issuing call\n    39→- **WHEN** agent issues a human call and other independent tasks exist\n    40→- **THEN** agent marks dependent tasks as waiting-human and continues other work\n    41→\n    42→### Requirement: Human Call Persistence\n    43→Async human call requests SHALL be persisted to the file system.\n    44→\n    45→Files stored in `human-calls/` with filename format `{YYYYMMDD}-{HHmmss}-{short-description}.md`.\n    46→\n    47→#### Scenario: Cross-session persistence\n    48→- **WHEN** session A's human call is unanswered at session end\n    49→- **THEN** the file persists and session B checks for responses on startup\n    50→\n    51→### Requirement: Human Call Types\n    52→The system SHALL support three types: decision, action, information.\n    53→\n    54→#### Scenario: Decision call\n    55→- **WHEN** agent needs the human to choose between options\n    56→- **THEN** the call lists all options with trade-off analysis\n    57→\n    58→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aa649a33-92f6-4c3e-90ea-c763bdcdac3a","uuid":"19a006ce-ad74-4f57-8f8f-ccd74a50cfba","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/data/cre/workspace/se3.0/openspec/specs/human-as-mcp/spec.md","content":"# human-as-mcp Specification\n\n## Purpose\nDefine the Human-as-MCP interface for obtaining human input on-demand. This spec governs sync and async human call modes, call persistence, non-blocking execution, and the first-time bootstrap flow where project intent is captured directly from human input without pre-written requirement files.\n## Requirements\n### Requirement: Human Call Interface\nThe system SHALL define a standard human call interface supporting sync and async modes.\n\n**Sync mode** (human present):\n- Ask directly via Claude Code conversation (AskUserQuestion)\n- Use for: immediate decisions, requirement clarification, project direction\n\n**Async mode** (human unavailable):\n- Write request file to `human-calls/`\n- Use for: offline operations, cross-session pending requests\n\n**First-time bootstrap**: When entering an empty project, the agent SHALL ask the human \"What should this project do?\" via sync human call, then create an openspec change directly from the response. The change proposal captures the human's intent; specs formalize it. No intermediate demands file.\n\n#### Scenario: Sync call — first-time project intent\n- **WHEN** agent enters an empty project\n- **THEN** agent asks the human via sync call, creates an openspec change proposal from the response\n\n#### Scenario: Sync call — immediate decision\n- **WHEN** agent needs a human decision and the human is present\n- **THEN** agent asks directly via conversation\n\n#### Scenario: Async call — offline operation\n- **WHEN** agent needs the human to perform an operation that requires offline time\n- **THEN** agent writes a request to human-calls/, marks dependent tasks as waiting-human\n\n#### Scenario: Human responds to async call\n- **WHEN** a human fills in the Response section of a pending request\n- **THEN** next session processes the response and unblocks dependent work\n\n### Requirement: Non-Blocking Execution\nHuman calls MUST NOT block unrelated tasks.\n\n#### Scenario: Continue after issuing call\n- **WHEN** agent issues a human call and other independent tasks exist\n- **THEN** agent marks dependent tasks as waiting-human and continues other work\n\n### Requirement: Human Call Persistence\nAsync human call requests SHALL be persisted to the file system.\n\nFiles stored in `human-calls/` with filename format `{YYYYMMDD}-{HHmmss}-{short-description}.md`.\n\n#### Scenario: Cross-session persistence\n- **WHEN** session A's human call is unanswered at session end\n- **THEN** the file persists and session B checks for responses on startup\n\n### Requirement: Human Call Types\nThe system SHALL support three types: decision, action, information.\n\n#### Scenario: Decision call\n- **WHEN** agent needs the human to choose between options\n- **THEN** the call lists all options with trade-off analysis\n\n","numLines":58,"startLine":1,"totalLines":58}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_h3lXWxYFhg1neq42zjZGyv0w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my analysis of the SE3 codebase, I can now create a comprehensive task plan for implementing the remaining SE3 functionality. The key areas are:\n\n1. **OpenSpec CLI Integration** - The session-protocol spec references `openspec init` and `openspec list` commands that don't exist\n2. **Spec Purpose Completion** - Three specs have \"TBD\" purposes\n3. **Human Call Archiving** - No archiving system for completed human calls\n4. **External Controller Cleanup** - Deprecated spec needs removal\n5. **Human Input Methods** - File-based input beyond MCP calls\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"plan\",\n  \"tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"task-001\",\n      \"branch\": \"collab/openspec-cli-commands\",\n      \"worktree\": \".worktrees/openspec-cli-commands\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement OpenSpec CLI commands (init, list)\",\n      \"prompt\": \"Implement the `openspec` CLI commands referenced in session-protocol spec but missing from the codebase.\\n\\n**Background**: The session-protocol spec (openspec/specs/session-protocol/spec.md) references `openspec init` and `openspec list --specs` commands in the startup protocol, but these commands don't exist. The se3 scaffold commands exist but not the openspec-specific commands.\\n\\n**What to implement**:\\n1. Add `openspec init` command - Initialize the openspec/ directory structure (similar to what se3 init does but focused on openspec/)\\n2. Add `openspec list --specs` command - List all available specs in openspec/specs/\\n\\n**Files to read**:\\n- openspec/specs/session-protocol/spec.md (lines 9-30 for startup protocol)\\n- openspec/specs/se3-scaffold/spec.md (for reference on init behavior)\\n- tools/se3_tools/commands/init.py (see how se3 init works)\\n- tools/se3_tools/cli.py (see CLI structure)\\n\\n**Implementation details**:\\n- The openspec commands can be subcommands of se3 OR a separate openspec CLI\\n- `openspec init` should create openspec/specs/, openspec/changes/, openspec/changes/archive/ directories\\n- `openspec list --specs` should list all specs in openspec/specs/ with their purposes\\n- Follow the existing command pattern in tools/se3_tools/commands/\\n\\n**Tests**: Add tests in tests/ directory following existing patterns.\\n\\n**Do NOT modify**: The session-protocol spec itself - only implement the missing commands it references.\",\n      \"spec_refs\": [\"openspec/specs/session-protocol/spec.md\", \"openspec/specs/se3-scaffold/spec.md\"],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"health\": {\n        \"timeout_minutes\": 60,\n        \"attempts\": 0,\n        \"max_attempts\": 3\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"task-002\",\n      \"branch\": \"collab/spec-purpose-updates\",\n      \"worktree\": \".worktrees/spec-purpose-updates\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"title\": \"Fill in TBD Purpose fields for three specs\",\n      \"prompt\": \"Update the Purpose fields for three specs that currently have \\\"TBD - created by archiving change\\\" placeholders.\\n\\n**Specs to update**:\\n1. **spec-lint** (openspec/specs/spec-lint/spec.md) - Currently line 4 has \\\"TBD - created by archiving change toolize-se3. Update Purpose after archive.\\\"\\n2. **requirement-intake** (openspec/specs/requirement-intake/spec.md) - Currently line 4 has \\\"TBD - created by archiving change requirement-capture. Update Purpose after archive.\\\"\\n3. **change-verifier** (openspec/specs/change-verifier/spec.md) - Currently line 4 has \\\"TBD - created by archiving change toolize-se3. Update Purpose after archive.\\\"\\n\\n**How to determine the Purpose**:\\nRead each spec's Requirements section and understand what it governs. Write a clear 1-2 sentence Purpose that explains:\\n- What this spec defines/controls\\n- Why it exists in the SE3 framework\\n\\n**Example good Purpose** (from session-protocol):\\n\\\"Define the session lifecycle protocol for SE 3.0 agents. This spec governs progressive startup, execution boundaries, shutdown procedures, and tool-enforced progress tracking across sessions.\\\"\\n\\n**Files to read**:\\n- openspec/specs/spec-lint/spec.md (read full file to understand its purpose)\\n- openspec/specs/requirement-intake/spec.md (read full file to understand its purpose)\\n- openspec/specs/change-verifier/spec.md (read full file to understand its purpose)\\n\\n**What to edit**:\\nOnly update the \\\"## Purpose\\\" section in each of the three spec files. Do not change any other content.\\n\\n**Verification**: Run `se3 lint` after changes to ensure specs are still valid.\",\n      \"spec_refs\": [\"openspec/specs/spec-lint/spec.md\", \"openspec/specs/requirement-intake/spec.md\", \"openspec/specs/change-verifier/spec.md\"],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"health\": {\n        \"timeout_minutes\": 30,\n        \"attempts\": 0,\n        \"max_attempts\": 3\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"task-003\",\n      \"branch\": \"collab/human-calls-archive\",\n      \"worktree\": \".worktrees/human-calls-archive\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement human calls archiving system\",\n      \"prompt\": \"Implement an archiving system for completed human calls.\\n\\n**Background**: The human-as-mcp spec defines async human calls stored in `human-calls/` directory. Currently there's no system to archive completed calls - they just accumulate in the main directory.\\n\\n**What to implement**:\\n1. Create `human-calls/archive/` directory structure\\n2. Add `se3 human-calls archive` command that:\\n   - Moves completed human calls (those with Response sections filled) to human-calls/archive/\\n   - Preserves the original filename format: `{YYYYMMDD}-{HHmmss}-{description}.md`\\n   - Optionally supports `--dry-run` to preview what would be archived\\n3. Add `se3 human-calls list` command that:\\n   - Lists pending (unresponded) human calls\\n   - Lists recently archived calls\\n4. Update `se3 collab --status` to show pending human calls count (mentioned in issues.md)\\n\\n**Files to read**:\\n- openspec/specs/human-as-mcp/spec.md (understand human call format)\\n- tools/se3_tools/human_calls.py (existing human call utilities)\\n- tools/se3_tools/commands/collab.py (see how --status works)\\n- tools/se3_tools/commands/status.py (for reference on status display)\\n\\n**Human call file format**:\\nFiles in human-calls/ have Request and Response sections. A call is \\\"completed\\\" when the Response section has content.\\n\\n**Implementation notes**:\\n- Add the new commands to tools/se3_tools/commands/ (create human_calls.py or similar)\\n- Register commands in cli.py\\n- Follow existing patterns for CLI output and error handling\\n- Add tests in tests/ directory\\n\\n**Do NOT modify**: The human-as-mcp spec itself - only implement the archiving functionality.\",\n      \"spec_refs\": [\"openspec/specs/human-as-mcp/spec.md\"],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"health\": {\n        \"timeout_minutes\": 60,\n        \"attempts\": 0,\n        \"max_attempts\": 3\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"task-004\",\n      \"branch\": \"collab/remove-external-controller\",\n      \"worktree\": \".worktrees/remove-external-controller\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"title\": \"Remove deprecated se3-controller spec\",\n      \"prompt\": \"Remove or archive the deprecated se3-controller spec.\\n\\n**Background**: The git-worktree-collab spec (v2) explicitly removed the External Controller architecture. The se3-controller spec is marked as experimental and deprecated. The git-worktree-collab spec states:\\n- \\\"Replace the experimental External Controller (v2)\\\"\\n- Lists REMOVED items: \\\"Python daemon process\\\", \\\"HTTP API server\\\", \\\"MCP server for manager-worker communication\\\"\\n\\n**What to do**:\\n1. Read the EXTERNAL-CONTROLLER-ARCH.md in openspec/specs/se3-controller/ to understand what it documented\\n2. Archive the se3-controller spec to openspec/changes/archive/ (similar to other archived changes)\\n3. Create an archive entry documenting that this was removed in favor of git-worktree-collab\\n4. Remove the se3-controller directory from openspec/specs/\\n\\n**Files to read**:\\n- openspec/specs/git-worktree-collab/spec.md (lines 30-45 for removal rationale)\\n- openspec/specs/se3-controller/spec.yaml (the OpenAPI spec)\\n- openspec/specs/se3-controller/EXTERNAL-CONTROLLER-ARCH.md\\n- openspec/changes/archive/ (see how other changes are archived for reference)\\n\\n**Archive format**:\\nFollow the pattern in openspec/changes/archive/:\\n- Create directory openspec/changes/archive/remove-se3-controller/\\n- Move the spec files there\\n- Add a CHANGE.md explaining why it was removed and what replaced it\\n\\n**Verification**: Ensure `se3 lint` still passes after removal.\",\n      \"spec_refs\": [\"openspec/specs/git-worktree-collab/spec.md\", \"openspec/specs/se3-controller/spec.yaml\"],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"health\": {\n        \"timeout_minutes\": 30,\n        \"attempts\": 0,\n        \"max_attempts\": 3\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"task-005\",\n      \"branch\": \"collab/human-input-methods\",\n      \"worktree\": \".worktrees/human-input-methods\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement file-based human input method\",\n      \"prompt\": \"Implement support for human input via prompt files as an alternative to MCP calls.\\n\\n**Background**: issues.md mentions: \\\"human从交互界面之外的输入方式，以及输入的归档\\\" (human input methods outside the interaction interface, and archiving of such input). This refers to supporting file-based human input in addition to sync/async MCP calls.\\n\\n**What to implement**:\\n1. Create `human-inputs/` directory structure for file-based human input\\n2. Add `se3 human input --file <path>` command that:\\n   - Reads a prompt file written by the human\\n   - Makes the content available to the agent\\n   - Archives the processed input file\\n3. Add `se3 human input --list` to show pending input files\\n4. Define the input file format (similar to human-calls but reversed - human writes request, agent responds)\\n\\n**File format for human inputs**:\\n```markdown\\n# Human Input: {title}\\n\\n## Context\\n{context provided by human}\\n\\n## Request\\n{what the human wants the agent to do}\\n\\n## Response\\n{agent fills this in}\\n```\\n\\n**Files to read**:\\n- openspec/specs/human-as-mcp/spec.md (understand existing human call patterns)\\n- tools/se3_tools/human_calls.py (existing patterns)\\n- tools/se3_tools/commands/ (see command structure)\\n\\n**Implementation notes**:\\n- This complements (not replaces) the existing human-as-mcp system\\n- Input files should be archived after processing (to human-inputs/archive/)\\n- Follow existing patterns for CLI commands\\n- Add tests in tests/ directory\\n\\n**Do NOT modify**: The human-as-mcp spec - this is an additional input method.\",\n      \"spec_refs\": [\"openspec/specs/human-as-mcp/spec.md\"],\n      \"dependencies\": [\"task-003\"],\n      \"health\": {\n        \"timeout_minutes\": 60,\n        \"attempts\": 0,\n        \"max_attempts\": 3\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"target_task\": \"\",\n  \"merge_branch\": \"\",\n  \"retry_prompt\": \"\",\n  \"reason\": \"Based on analysis of the SE3 codebase, I identified 5 key areas of remaining functionality: 1) OpenSpec CLI commands referenced in session-protocol but not implemented, 2) Three specs with TBD Purpose fields, 3) No human calls archiving system, 4) Deprecated se3-controller spec needs removal, 5) File-based human input method not implemented. Tasks 1-4 are independent and can run in parallel. Task 5 depends on task 3 (human calls archive system) as it shares similar patterns.\",\n  \"summary\": \"Created 5 tasks for remaining SE3 functionality: OpenSpec CLI, spec purposes, human calls archive, remove deprecated controller, file-based human input\"\n}\n```"}],"model":"kimi-for-coding","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":34421,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard","prompt_tokens":34421,"cached_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aa649a33-92f6-4c3e-90ea-c763bdcdac3a","uuid":"f9b400f1-292e-4552-91fa-68fd8475c9ce"}
